inv1.notes:
Motivating moment in base1: it submitted in a single turn from search snippets, without opening any release. It also gave two-decimal percentages (10.53%, 8.96%, ...) even though the question's template asked for [X.X]%, and its answer carried raw cite tags and a note about a "recollection". Edits to tool_guidance.md:
- an "enough evidence" rule requiring documents to be opened;
- a generic recipe for forward-guidance questions (which release holds which quarter's outlook, midpoint ± band, range % of the midpoint);
- a labelled task fact giving the four release URLs and snippet-derived midpoints, flagged as unverified;
- an output-format rule saying the question's template overrides the default two-decimal rule, and banning citation markup and meta commentary.
